# Findings in the pinned runtime image that are accepted rather than fixed.
#
# Passed to Trivy by scripts/security/lib.sh. One finding identifier per line,
# followed by exp:YYYY-MM-DD, under a comment naming the exception that argues
# it. Every identifier here is an accepted exception in
# docs/security/security-baseline.v1alpha1.json and
# docs/security/deferred-risks.md, and tests/security/ refuses an identifier no
# exception names, an exception naming one that is not here, and an expiry that
# is not the exception's review deadline.
#
# Each finding was assessed against the image named below and no other. The
# guard refuses to scan when the runtime contract pins a different image, so a
# rotated pin cannot inherit an exception argued for the old bytes.
#
# assessed-image: ghcr.io/ggml-org/llama.cpp@sha256:100de626bdc5b7df898c12561eefaf557019d2746d5fc8d3f4d7fd24e15ad384
#
# On its expiry date Trivy stops suppressing an entry and the finding blocks
# again. An entry suppresses its finding for every package in the image it is
# reported against, and the scan output still records it, under
# ExperimentalModifiedFindings, because the guard passes --show-suppressed.

# EX-07: OpenSSL DTLS retransmission out-of-bounds read, in openssl and libssl3t64.
CVE-2026-84782 exp:2026-10-30
